From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:12:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] camera: expose samsung 60fps video modes

the samsung hal keeps its 60fps video modes in its own video
configuration tags, so standard camera apps only see 30fps. expose the
60fps ae range and matching stream min frame durations up to the sizes
the hal lists.

the hal only enters its 60fps sensor mode when the target fps rises
past 30 and loses it on every reconfigure, so cap the first request
after a reconfigure to 30fps and let the next one restart the mode.
sessions outside 16:9 stay at 30fps since the hal has no 60fps sensor
mode for other aspect ratios.
